  "solution": "The pattern followed here is:\n\nWe have to interchange the given numbers in the options and find which option is correct.\n\n**Given: **14 + 39 - ( sqrt{144} ÷ 4 ) + ( 5 × 3 ) - 6 = 63\n\nLet's check each option one by one:\n\n**Option 1) **14 and 6\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get the:\n\n⇒ 6 + 39 - __**( **____**sqrt{144}**____** ÷ 4 )**__ + ( 5 × 3 ) - 14 = 63\n\n⇒ 6 + 39 - __**(12 ÷ 4)**__ + __**(5 × 3)**__ - 14 = 63\n\n⇒ __**6 + 39**__ - 3 __**+ 15**__ - 14 = 63\n\n⇒ __**60 - 3 - 14**__ = 63\n\n⇒ 43 ≠ 63\n\n**⇒ ****LHS ≠ RHS**\n\n**Option 2) **5 and 39\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get the:\n\n⇒ 14 + 5 - __**( **____**sqrt{144}**____** ÷ 4)**__ + __**(39 × 3) **__- 6 = 63\n\n⇒ 14 + 5 - __**(12 ÷ 4)**__ + __**(39 × 3)**__ - 6 = 63\n\n⇒ __**14 + 5**__ - 3 __**+ 117**__ - 6 = 63\n\n⇒ __**136 - 3 - 6**__ = 63\n\n⇒ 127 ≠ 63\n\n⇒ **LHS ≠ RHS**\n\n**Option 3) **4 and 3\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get the:\n\n⇒ 14 + 39 - __**( **____**sqrt{144}**____** ÷ 3)**__ + __**( 5 × 4)**__ - 6 = 63\n\n⇒ 14 + 39 - __**(12 ÷ 3)**__ + __**(5 × 4)**__ - 6 = 63\n\n⇒ __**14 + 39**__ - 4 __**+ 20**__ - 6 = 63\n\n⇒ __**73 - 4 - 6**__ = 63\n\n⇒ 63 = 63\n\n⇒ **LHS = RHS**\n\n**Option 4) **4 and 6\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get the:\n\n⇒ 14 + 39 -__** (**____**sqrt{144}**____** ÷ 6)**__ + __**(5 × 3 )**__ - 4 = 63\n\n⇒ 14 + 39 - __**(12 ÷ 6)**__ + __**(5 × 3)**__ - 4 = 63\n\n⇒ __**14 + 39**__ - 2 __**+ 15**__ - 4 = 63\n\n⇒ __**68 - 2 - 4**__ = 63\n\n⇒ 62 ≠ 63\n\n⇒ **LHS ≠ RHS**\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"Option 3\".**",
